{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990235-limits-scale-adjustments-for-wonderful-machine","id":990235,"title":"Limits/scale/adjustments for Wonderful Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-19T20:43:39-07:00","id":990235,"title":"Limits/scale/adjustments for Wonderful Machine","content":"Just wondering, what is the maximum scope of what you can change with Wonderful Machine? Can you turn a pile of junked cars into a supersonic jet? What can you do to make the transformation permanent, if it isn't already, or expand the scope to be able to do that? <br /> <br /> And could you compensate for lack of sufficient parts using other arcana? So, for example, making Forces-powered engines or a Forces-powered cloaking device (since you don't want paradox backlash when you're miles above the earth moving at supersonic speed)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:23:05-07:00","id":991683,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to combine it with Mind to put an AI in the creation? With Life to make shapeshifting cybernetics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:59:27-07:00","id":991695,"title":"","content":"To provide erudition. You can add aspects of one thing to another. No. Yes. The scope of time is based on the duration factors used in the spell, indefinite is possible but very difficult to achieve. Not as written in the Rote so these would be things to add with seperate spells or by improvising the spell and combining the other effects with the spell you are creating. There is already a mind spell for creating a new consciousness, I'd argue is MI rather than AI since you didn't create it artificially but with magic. Lastly, I'm not sure where you see Life being part of shapeshifting cybernetics. Life might allow you to add the artificial parts to yourself without making you die from the dodgy surgery, but magic isn't needed for a real world pacemaker to work inside someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T21:00:57-07:00","id":991697,"title":"","content":"I don't mean Life for a pacemaker, I mean Life to be able to take a hunk of metal, turn it into an arm, then connect fhe arm to your body and have it work.<br /> <br /> So, what would it take to turn a pile of scrap metal into a jet-powered VTOL?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T21:09:13-07:00","id":991699,"title":"","content":"What's the distinction between a prosthetic arm made in a lab/factory and one made with magic beyond the actual fabrication? As I said, life may be needed to attach the limb successfully, but by definition, a robotic limb is not alive. If you are talking about turn a table into a flesh arm and attaching it to yourself, then yes, you would need life and matter to change the table into flesh and then attach it. Changing scrap metal into a jet would require a higher level of matter than Wonderful Machine, Wonderful Machine describes what it does, it combines to items to add the effect of one item to another. In the case of scrap metal and scrap metal, I believe you could add additional rust. To make a vtol you'd need something that's basically already a vtol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T21:31:31-07:00","id":991704,"title":"","content":"To make a Vtol you'd need to use Wonderful Machine on a plane and a helicopter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:07:29-07:00","id":991742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990235-limits-scale-adjustments-for-wonderful-machine#post990235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering, what is the maximum scope of what you can change with Wonderful Machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Potency properties from other things can be melded onto a single thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you turn a pile of junked cars into a supersonic jet? </div> </div> </div>No, junked cars do not have the properties of a supersonic jet. You cannot create new properties, just copy existing ones to something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What can you do to make the transformation permanent, if it isn't already, or expand the scope to be able to do that? </div> </div> </div>Add Advanced Duration (one reach or one mana with the Matter 2 Attainment) and Indefinite duration (an additional one reach and one mana).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And could you compensate for lack of sufficient parts using other arcana? </div> </div> </div>No, that requires Imbued Item or casting the spell directly. If it's cast directly you probably don't want to relinquish control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:49:52-08:00","id":1001779,"title":"","content":"As a follow up to this question... what happens with the machines that are &quot;superimposed? To they actually meld together and become a single frankenstein amalgamation of the component machines, can the looks be dictated by the spell or is it just machines fusing together? or is this more of a drawing together of Supernal concepts that impart the attributes? which leaves the original donor machine without that property for the duration of the spell and the new machine with all of the properties imposed on it for the duration? IF Supernal, does it change the look at all beyond the minimum required to produce the effect or even that? Say a Bear trap / Blowtorch's flame jet, would the bear trap need the hole for the flame to come out or would it just have a gout of flame coming out?<br /> <br /> If this is a cast at sensory and this is a melding, do the component machines &quot;fly&quot; into each other to form a single device?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:51:47-08:00","id":1001780,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much up to narration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:02:08-08:00","id":1002321,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, that is a less than ideal answer for my group's mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T15:48:13-08:00","id":1002386,"title":"","content":"Why is that? Anyways, just pick an answer you like and it can just work like that every time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T20:32:07-08:00","id":1002755,"title":"","content":"Which is what I am going to do, As for the ideal answer, my group always prefers to have RAW spell things out<br /> <br /> It seems to make more sense (at least in a pedantic way, anyway) for me to err on the side of the &quot;superimpose pieces of various objects&quot; effect should physically blend the parts of things together into a single device. (Plus visually, that would be so much more striking<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) and if they want to hide a machine into another that can just be one of the qualities that they superimpose. If done at a distance, then the parts will morph resemble those traits (unless specified not to).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T02:55:17-08:00","id":1002809,"title":"","content":"RAW is fine for rules mechanics, but it makes no mechanical difference, does it? I don't think I'd want the book to spell out my descriptions for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T05:39:14-08:00","id":1002845,"title":"","content":"I'd say it does make a difference really. If a car driving down the road is merged with a traffic light (say giving the light the quality of locomotion), what happens to the car? Does it teleport up to the lightbox? Does it just low down naturally? What about the passenger?<br /> <br /> Does this destroy the original objects? It means more resources must be spent to purchase the original items again. Time could be spent to fix the original objects if it's a physical change. If it's a supernal quality swap, sleepers have no idea what's going on as the objects look to be functioning normally but that danged engine just isn't running. One casting is subtle while the other is grossly magical. <br /> <br /> One example has the possibility of teleporting parts or machines flying through the air (when cast at sensory in particular) while the other leaves them wholly intact and appearing normal. <br /> <br /> I'd go with the idea that the qualities are what exchange spots, interweaving the supernal patterns of the items in a way that exchanges or reflects the other qualities. It becomes a metaphysical change instead of a physical one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5951,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5951-cayros","user":"Cayros","date":".  clarification 11-14-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5951-cayros","name":"Cayros","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T05:52:58-08:00","id":1002848,"title":"","content":"Well, I would say that after the spell ends, both objects are back to their original state. I like to imagine that you are not actually doing &quot;science&quot; of combining these items; you are literally installing a gun inside a pen, you are looking symbolical construction of Gun, borrowing some of these qualities that make Gun-a-Gun, and then literally slap them together with similarly borrowed symbols from another object. Reality then scratches it's head and renders your probably nonsensical design, expressing it as closest to making sense as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T09:15:00-08:00","id":1002918,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, verdana, sans-serif\">So Cayros beat me to this a bit. If mechanics are not clear on the idea of whether some environmental effects take place because of the description. Such as flying parts interfering with people's actions.</span> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> - Exactly my issue with it as written. Its not clear on the state of the components being used. I mean is it stealing or copying just the desired supernal quality from an object, or is it physically pushing them together. All of these options have implications, either you are able to double up some device or you have an effective way of disabling another machine or as above you have another way of creating environmental conditions as the side-effect of a spell that I don't think was intended to do so.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T09:17:43-08:00","id":1002920,"title":"","content":"I'd just cover that stuff under the narrative effects that d spells as mentioned in the spellcasting section. As such they don't necessarily need to be standardized, and on top of that you can pick how it's going to affect the environment? Or whether it disables machines it's drawing from or whatever when the player states their intent for the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T09:56:14-08:00","id":1002934,"title":"","content":"So I'd suppose a spell that disables one machine and empowers another would need to go against the withstand of the disabled machine. Without the disabling effect, it would simply be replicating the abilities of another device.<br /> <br /> Spending scale would allow you to make multiple duplications of one copied property then. Ex:5 pens now that the ability to generate heat like that roaster over there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5951-cayros","name":"Cayros","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}